  "result": "I added the `docs-writer` subagent in `.claude/agents/docs-writer.md`, following the same format as the existing agents.\n\n- **Tools:** it gets `Read, Grep, Glob, Edit, Write`. Bash isn't on the list, so it can't run shell commands.\n- **Model:** `haiku`, the fastest one.\n- **Instructions:** it only edits Markdown under `docs/` and reads the relevant code before documenting it. Like the project rules, it refers to secrets as `${VAR}`.\n\nThe \"only under `docs/`\" limit is just an instruction in the prompt. Nothing technically stops it from writing elsewhere. If you want that enforced, a hook could block edits outside `docs/`, like the existing `block-rm.mjs` hook does for `rm`.\n\nI didn't run `npm run lint` or `npm run build`, because this change only adds a config file and no app code.",
